Subject: [PATCH] agent: remember the discovered controller before WSC

On a virgin controller, all initial M1 frames can arrive before its queued
agent data-model commit completes and be discarded. The bounded M1 retry
uses get_peer_mac(), but the selected controller address has not yet been
stored in the agent network model when no M2 has been received. Its first
M1 uses the response Ethernet source directly, masking this on warm labs
or when any band receives M2 on the first attempt.

Persist the controller AL address from the validated, non-DPP autoconfig
response before starting WSC. Retries then address the same controller even
when every initial M1 is lost. No retry delays, limits or discovery policy
are changed, and no deployment-side restart workaround is required.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
+++ b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
@@ -6463,6 +6463,7 @@ int em_configuration_t::handle_autoconfig_resp(unsigned char *buff, unsigned int len)
     }
 
     printf("Received resp and validated...creating M1 msg\n");
+    get_data_model()->set_ctrl_al_interface_mac(hdr->src);
     int msg_len = create_autoconfig_wsc_m1_msg(msg, hdr->src);
     if (msg_len < 0) {
         em_printfout("Error: Failed to create autoconfig wsc m1 msg");
